    "standardized_narrative": "The Syndicate experienced a net strengthening of prior year gross claims reserves by GBP 1.525 million in 2022, calculated from the claims development triangle. This movement is consistent with the reported loss of GBP 1.5 million for the 2020 and prior underwriting years. A specific strengthening of GBP 5.6 million was recorded as an additional risk premium above the core best estimate reserve to close the 2020 year of account into the 2021 year. The reserving process explicitly considered economic and excess inflation, leading to adjustments in outstanding claims and IBNR claims. The Syndicate also adopted new reserve methodologies, including uplifting outstanding claims reserves by a set factor and uplifting IBNR expected loss ratios.",
